Expose nl80211 mgmt_tx so AP mode works with wpa_supplicant 2.12

wpa_supplicant 2.12 dropped the monitor-interface fallback that 2.11
used on full-MAC radios (the atbm6041 does not support
NL80211_CMD_REGISTER_FRAME, so AP mode previously relied on a monitor
iface to carry auth frames). With 2.12 the only path is nl80211 frame
registration, which kernel 3.10 rejects with EOPNOTSUPP unless the
driver implements .mgmt_tx.

Expose ieee80211_mgmt_tx() and the ROC machinery it depends on without
enabling the P2P feature that used to gate all of it:
- cfg.c: compile the mgmt_tx/ROC block and its ops-table entries when
  CONFIG_ATBM_MGMT_TX is set (previously only under CONFIG_ATBM_SUPPORT_P2P)
- ieee80211_i.h: un-gate the ROC struct fields (roc_list, hw_roc_*,
  roc_cookie*) and the off-channel/ROC prototypes
- scan.c: un-gate ieee80211_run_pending_scan, called from offchannel.c
- offchannel.c: the whole file (ROC workqueue helpers) was wrapped in
  CONFIG_ATBM_SUPPORT_P2P; include it under CONFIG_ATBM_MGMT_TX too
- main.c: call ieee80211_hw_roc_setup() (INIT_LIST_HEAD of local->roc_list)
  for MGMT_TX builds too -- without it the list head is NULL and
  list_empty() in mgmt_tx walks it and crashes
- Makefile: define CONFIG_ATBM_MGMT_TX and always build offchannel.o

P2P itself stays disabled; the P2P iftype cases inside mgmt_tx compile
out as before.

diff --git a/hal_apollo/Makefile b/hal_apollo/Makefile
index ae11dea..2a3bd86 100644
--- a/hal_apollo/Makefile
+++ b/hal_apollo/Makefile
@@ -87,7 +87,12 @@ ccflags-y += -DATBM_CHANGE_AP_TIMESTAMP_TO_BOOTTIME
 ccflags-y += -DATBM_FUNCTION
 #ccflags-y += -DATBM_USE_SAVED_FW
 #ccflags-y += -DATBM_AP_SME
-#ccflags-y += -DP2P_MULTIVIF
+#ccflags-y += -DP2P_MULTIVIF
+# Expose nl80211 mgmt_tx so AP mode works with wpa_supplicant >= 2.12.
+# The kernel rejects NL80211_CMD_REGISTER_FRAME unless the driver has
+# .mgmt_tx; wpa_supplicant 2.12 dropped the monitor-interface fallback
+# that 2.11 used on full-MAC radios like this one.
+ccflags-y += -DCONFIG_ATBM_MGMT_TX
 ccflags-y += -DATBM_P2P_CHANGE
 ccflags-y += -DATBM_WIFI_NO_P2P_PS
 ccflags-y += -DATBM_SPECIAL_PKG_DOWN_RATE
@@ -546,7 +551,9 @@ $(ATBM_MODULES_NAME)-$(APSME)    += mac80211/ap_sme.o
 $(ATBM_MODULES_NAME)-$(MICREPORT)    += mac80211/event.o
 $(ATBM_MODULES_NAME)-$(SPECTRUMMGMT) += mac80211/spectmgmt.o
 $(ATBM_MODULES_NAME)-$(IBSSENABLE) += mac80211/ibss.o
-$(ATBM_MODULES_NAME)-$(P2PENABLE) += mac80211/offchannel.o
+# offchannel.o provides the ROC helpers (ieee80211_sw_roc_work etc.)
+# that ieee80211_mgmt_tx() needs, so build it even without P2P.
+$(ATBM_MODULES_NAME)-y += mac80211/offchannel.o
 $(ATBM_MODULES_NAME)-$(BRIDGE) += mac80211/bridge.o
 $(ATBM_MODULES_NAME)-$(MEM_DEBUG) += mac80211/ieee80211_atbm_mem.o
 $(ATBM_MODULES_NAME)-$(SKB_DEBUG) += mac80211/ieee80211_atbm_skb.o
